course: dictionary
lesson: 16186
title: Yummy and its friends
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Yummy is a fun, everyday word. It is informal, which means you use it when you chat with friends and family, not usually in a school essay. Its main meaning is tasting very good. «This cake is yummy!» tells you the cake is delicious.
explain: Yummy can also mean very attractive or pleasant. Look at the clues around the word. Food words like cake, soup or pizza tell you it means tasty. Words about things to look at, like sunsets, tell you it means lovely to see.
explain: In a formal text, swap yummy for delicious or tasty. «The meal was delicious» sounds more grown-up than «The meal was yummy». Use the swap test: put your word into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Yummy can also be a shout. «Yum!» or «Yummy!» can be said on its own when you smell or taste something good. These are interjections, and they show feeling.
fact: Yummy is an informal word, so use it in chats and stories, and use «delicious» or «tasty» in formal writing.
fact: «Yummy» means tasting very good, or delicious.
fact: «Yummy» can also mean very attractive or pleasant, as in «The sunset looked yummy over the sea.»
fact: The forms are yummier and yummiest: «This soup is yummier than the last one.»
fact: «Yum!» and «Yummy!» can be said on their own to show you enjoy something.
exercise: «This cake is yummy!» What does yummy mean here? | Very cold | Very heavy | Very noisy | *Tastes very good
exercise: Ella says, «Yum!» as the pizza arrives. What is she showing? | She is angry with the waiter | She is sleepy | *She enjoys the smell and taste of the food | She wants to leave the table
exercise: Which word would be best in a formal school essay instead of yummy? | messy | *delicious | noisy | yucky
test: «The soup smelled yummy, so Jack had a big bowl.» What does yummy mean? | Made of metal | Smelled bad | Very hot and steamy | *Very good to eat
test: Which word is the comparative form of yummy? | yumminess | yum | *yummier | yummiest
exam: «The sunset looked yummy over the sea.» Which meaning fits best here? | Tasting very good | Very noisy | *Very attractive or pleasant to look at | Cold and wet
